The legal texts in this repository are Nigerian federal legislation, as printed and published by the Federal
Government Printer, Lagos, in supplements to the Official Gazette of the Federal Republic of Nigeria, and the
Constitution of the Federal Republic of Nigeria, 1999, as printed by the Federal Ministry of Justice, Abuja. Each
act's gazette, and the government website whose copy was used, is listed in README.md and REPRODUCE.md (with its
sha256).

Official texts of legislation are not protected by copyright in Nigeria. Copyright Act, 2022 (Act No. 8 of 2022),
section 3: "The following shall not be eligible for copyright — ... (b) official texts of a legislative or
administrative nature as well as any official translations, except their compilations". Each act here was read
from its own printed text, not from a compilation.

The copies used state no licence of their own.

Changes made by Lexifina: each act was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per line;
spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; the printer's side notes were used as section headings, and Part and
Chapter headings and cross-reference side notes were left out; the versions were arranged as git commits credited
to the laws that made them. The wording of the law was not changed. Neither the Federal Government Printer, the
Federal Ministry of Justice nor any website named in README.md endorses this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
